WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.057 --> 00:00:02.640
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.542 --> 00:00:07.942
- It's a culture in New York City.

00:00:07.942 --> 00:00:12.902
Basketball is in every
borough, in every community.

00:00:12.902 --> 00:00:14.086
Basketball hoops are a big part

00:00:14.086 --> 00:00:16.316
about the youth of New York City.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:19.574
You can go to a park by
yourself with a basketball.

00:00:19.574 --> 00:00:20.763
You don't need nobody else.

00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:23.037
You can go with two people,
you can go with four people,

00:00:23.037 --> 00:00:25.399
and you know, it keeps
the kids off the street,

00:00:25.399 --> 00:00:26.946
keeps them maybe out
of trouble and it might

00:00:26.946 --> 00:00:30.447
give them something to look forward to.

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:31.708
- [Voiceover] John and
his fellow blacksmiths

00:00:31.708 --> 00:00:34.396
of the New York City Parks
Department make and repair

00:00:34.396 --> 00:00:37.829
everything from lock
boxes to lifeguard chairs.

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:40.233
But some of their most
icon work is hand-making

00:00:40.233 --> 00:00:42.266
the basketball hoops in many of

00:00:42.266 --> 00:00:44.992
the city's parks and playgrounds.

00:00:44.992 --> 00:00:47.742
(metal clanging)

00:00:50.604 --> 00:00:54.121
This is the long start
that's actually the rim.

00:00:54.121 --> 00:00:58.288
It's 5/8 inches in diameter,
it's 58 9/16 in length.

00:00:59.372 --> 00:01:01.734
Put initial bend in the first four inches

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:05.458
then we put it in the roller and roll it.

00:01:05.458 --> 00:01:08.041
(upbeat music)

00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:11.004
Every one of these hoops are made

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:13.078
like they're individual hoops.

00:01:13.078 --> 00:01:16.332
You know, none of them
are exactly the same.

00:01:16.332 --> 00:01:17.836
I believe there's a value in making them

00:01:17.836 --> 00:01:21.785
because the quality is much
better than what you can buy.

00:01:21.785 --> 00:01:23.144
We made one of these originally

00:01:23.144 --> 00:01:26.278
back in, I think back in 1994, '95.

00:01:26.278 --> 00:01:30.347
Over the years I probably
made over, maybe 1000 rims.

00:01:30.347 --> 00:01:32.549
This is your final product, New York City

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:35.216
Parks Department basketball rim.

00:01:37.144 --> 00:01:38.493
- [Voiceover] Over the course of a year,

00:01:38.493 --> 00:01:40.944
John and other blacksmiths
craft and replace

00:01:40.944 --> 00:01:44.326
up to 100 rims throughout
the city's courts.

00:01:44.326 --> 00:01:45.832
They're made by city workers and they're

00:01:45.832 --> 00:01:47.828
being played by city kids.

00:01:47.828 --> 00:01:50.411
What's more New York than that?

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:54.093
I watch college basketball
and you always hear

00:01:54.093 --> 00:01:55.560
all these colleges around the country,

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.328
this kid is from Brooklyn,
this kid is from the Bronx.

00:01:58.328 --> 00:02:00.284
So probably in their playing
days, someplace along

00:02:00.284 --> 00:02:02.812
the way, they all played
on New York City rims.

00:02:02.812 --> 00:02:04.562
And it probably was a help in the process

00:02:04.562 --> 00:02:07.145
of them making what they were.

